Proposed patch (NOT applied; the L1 decides). Target: tools/battery-discrimination-r88.py at
1fac4195243e55e7d9d8a2eddd653443d8559bff.

Defect (observable): the docstring of tools/battery-discrimination-r88.py, lines 11-12, says
  "void (exit 2) if this file or any roster file differs from
   `.ufo/waves/round-88/before/freeze-manifest.sha256` / the roster digests"
and the round-88 declaration's C1 kill rule says "void if the counter or any roster file differs
from .ufo/waves/round-88/before/freeze-manifest.sha256". The code never reads the manifest:
`grep -n freeze tools/battery-discrimination-r88.py` matches only that docstring line (12).
load_roster() (lines 51-62) compares each gate file to the digest stored *inside* roster-r88.json,
so a roster-r88.json edited with internally consistent digests - or the counter's own edited copy -
runs instead of voiding. The receipt records counter_sha256/roster_sha256 (line 158-160), so an
external auditor can still catch it; the instrument itself does not, which is what the docstring
and the kill rule promise.

Minimal patch: read the manifest once, check the counter, roster-r88.json and every frozen roster
gate against it, and void (exit 2) before any gate runs.

